1
00:00:10,944 --> 00:00:13,947
In the missing persons case
of Mt. Shikara in Hokkaido,

2
00:00:14,014 --> 00:00:18,184
three of the missing were members
of a joint operation,

3
00:00:18,251 --> 00:00:20,620
working on a drug investigation.

4
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:24,624
Last year, a highly lethal drug
was widely circulated.

5
00:00:25,225 --> 00:00:26,426
It goes by the name "CAN-d."

6
00:00:26,493 --> 00:00:29,996
They were after Motoka Tabatake,
thought to be a courier.

7
00:00:30,964 --> 00:00:32,999
It was found in our club room.

8
00:00:33,066 --> 00:00:34,134
"CAN-d."

9
00:00:35,502 --> 00:00:38,972
No matter the results,
you mustn't tell anyone but me.

10
00:00:40,907 --> 00:00:43,476
A normal person
can't earn this much a month.

11
00:00:43,543 --> 00:00:47,914
Do you know how Ms. Tabatake
paid this astronomical amount?

12
00:00:47,981 --> 00:00:51,985
If the family can afford it,
we doctors will respect their wishes.

13
00:00:54,354 --> 00:00:56,356
You're not thinking of doing
something shady, are you?

14
00:00:56,856 --> 00:00:59,459
Is this notebook my sister's?

15
00:01:03,696 --> 00:01:05,765
Nono, who suffers
from an incurable disease…

16
00:01:06,332 --> 00:01:09,769
Can she receive the life insurance money?

17
00:01:10,870 --> 00:01:14,574
Her mother's savings can only cover
four months' worth of treatment.

18
00:01:16,743 --> 00:01:18,178
Examine her again in an hour.

19
00:01:18,244 --> 00:01:19,145
Yes.

20
00:01:21,114 --> 00:01:23,416
Her breathing is stable for now.

21
00:01:23,483 --> 00:01:25,885
She hasn't been sleeping well lately.

22
00:01:25,952 --> 00:01:28,755
We are watching her carefully.
Please don't worry.

23
00:01:43,770 --> 00:01:45,105
I won't give up.

24
00:01:45,171 --> 00:01:49,476
I'll do everything I can
so that the life insurance can be paid.

25
00:01:50,276 --> 00:01:53,279
Even if the chance is 0.00001%.

26
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:55,315
-Here.
-Thank you.

27
00:02:06,326 --> 00:02:08,094
Nao, your daughter…

28
00:02:08,895 --> 00:02:10,497
Did she also get fevers often?

29
00:02:11,164 --> 00:02:12,899
She caught colds easily.

30
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:15,168
We often took her
to the hospital at night.

31
00:02:16,402 --> 00:02:19,506
Is the expensive medicine
just not working for Nono?

32
00:02:21,107 --> 00:02:24,544
If gene therapy isn't started
within four months…

33
00:02:24,611 --> 00:02:25,578
Then?

34
00:02:25,645 --> 00:02:27,213
What happens?

35
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:32,185
At worst, she dies.

36
00:02:38,124 --> 00:02:41,427
-Sorry for making you come along.
-I don't have work until tomorrow.

37
00:02:43,429 --> 00:02:45,732
I'll investigate Ms. Tabatake thoroughly.

38
00:02:47,333 --> 00:02:49,435
I have to keep my promise to Nono.

39
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:55,708
Ogoma.

40
00:02:55,775 --> 00:02:56,743
Yes?

41
00:02:56,809 --> 00:02:59,612
Haven't you been warned
not to investigate independently?

42
00:03:00,146 --> 00:03:02,182
And do only what you're told.

43
00:03:05,485 --> 00:03:07,520
Didn't your company tell you the same?

44
00:03:08,821 --> 00:03:10,657
Are you only doing what you're told?

45
00:03:11,457 --> 00:03:14,360
-I'm only doing what I was told.
-Mr. Nao.

46
00:03:16,729 --> 00:03:17,830
Let's talk frankly.

47
00:03:17,897 --> 00:03:19,199
I'm always frank.

48
00:03:19,933 --> 00:03:22,435
Then let's talk money.

49
00:03:23,503 --> 00:03:26,806
To save Nono, is there no other way
than the life insurance money?

50
00:03:27,440 --> 00:03:28,341
Something more realistic?

51
00:03:28,408 --> 00:03:32,779
Nothing is more realistic
than her mom's life insurance.

52
00:03:34,781 --> 00:03:38,151
Once the claim goes through,
30 million yen will definitely come in.

53
00:03:39,152 --> 00:03:41,721
Gene therapy is expensive.

54
00:03:41,788 --> 00:03:43,289
If it can help with that…

55
00:03:47,093 --> 00:03:49,295
You won't make
a fraudulent claim, will you?

56
00:03:50,196 --> 00:03:53,499
That's the same as scamming
the company for 30 million yen.

57
00:03:58,171 --> 00:04:00,039
You've matured.

58
00:04:00,974 --> 00:04:02,375
Doubt everything.

59
00:04:02,442 --> 00:04:04,944
I'm telling you.
Don't go crossing any lines!

60
00:04:06,946 --> 00:04:08,281
See you.

61
00:04:17,857 --> 00:04:19,826
Ms. Saruwatari. Please follow me.

62
00:04:22,795 --> 00:04:24,063
Hello.

63
00:04:26,466 --> 00:04:27,333
They're over there.

64
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:28,401
Thank you.

65
00:04:28,468 --> 00:04:29,302
Hello.

66
00:04:29,369 --> 00:04:31,070
-Sorry for making you wait.
-It's fine.

67
00:04:32,171 --> 00:04:33,006
What's all that?

68
00:04:34,607 --> 00:04:36,576
Why so much? Whoa!

69
00:04:36,643 --> 00:04:39,545
I made a strange request,
so this is a thank you.

70
00:04:41,914 --> 00:04:42,682
Yummy.

71
00:04:44,851 --> 00:04:46,786
-How were the results?
-Let's eat first.

72
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:48,588
Let's talk first.

73
00:04:59,932 --> 00:05:01,601
You should consult the police.

74
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:05,738
Is this all you found?

75
00:05:07,907 --> 00:05:08,574
Yes.

76
00:05:11,611 --> 00:05:12,478
Here.

77
00:05:19,218 --> 00:05:20,453
Is this accurate?

78
00:05:29,762 --> 00:05:34,367
I want to report in detail
what happened in Tokyo.

79
00:05:34,434 --> 00:05:35,301
Yeah?

80
00:05:37,870 --> 00:05:38,738
But I can't.

81
00:05:38,805 --> 00:05:41,607
That talk about you sticking your nose
into a secret investigation was true?

82
00:05:41,674 --> 00:05:43,209
You idiot.

83
00:05:43,276 --> 00:05:46,913
But thanks to your support,
I didn't come home empty-handed.

84
00:05:46,979 --> 00:05:47,947
Thanks!

85
00:05:48,548 --> 00:05:50,583
If you're satisfied, it's all good.

86
00:05:51,417 --> 00:05:53,953
I always found this case strange.

87
00:05:54,487 --> 00:05:57,156
If there's a secret investigation.
It all makes sense.

88
00:05:58,224 --> 00:06:01,728
We are all police. Why can't we
just help each other out?

89
00:06:02,428 --> 00:06:03,596
Oh, that's mine!

90
00:06:03,663 --> 00:06:04,797
I took care of it.

91
00:06:04,864 --> 00:06:07,367
Even inside the police,
there are turf fights.

92
00:06:07,433 --> 00:06:10,536
We don't reveal cases
that could earn credit for other units.

93
00:06:10,603 --> 00:06:14,140
The higher up you go, the more serious
the cases, the more true this is.

94
00:06:15,708 --> 00:06:18,578
Just tell me whether
you found Harune or not.

95
00:06:21,114 --> 00:06:21,948
I see.

96
00:06:24,817 --> 00:06:26,853
This tastes different from usual.

97
00:06:30,022 --> 00:06:30,857
Really?

98
00:06:36,729 --> 00:06:40,867
Did you look more into Nikaido and Harune?

99
00:06:42,001 --> 00:06:43,102
Nikaido.

100
00:06:43,836 --> 00:06:45,138
Around 2010,

101
00:06:45,738 --> 00:06:48,408
he was associated
with a quasi-gang in Susukino.

102
00:06:49,175 --> 00:06:51,911
That's why HQ was onto him.

103
00:06:55,782 --> 00:06:59,485
His deposits and withdrawals
match the restaurant's sales.

104
00:06:59,552 --> 00:07:01,287
No suspicious money flow.

105
00:07:01,921 --> 00:07:05,591
But he did act as a labor broker
to make pocket money.

106
00:07:06,125 --> 00:07:07,794
Is it sex work?

107
00:07:07,860 --> 00:07:09,295
Was he selling women?

108
00:07:09,362 --> 00:07:13,466
He introduced people who were struggling
to farms and factories that needed labor,

109
00:07:13,533 --> 00:07:14,934
and took a margin.

110
00:07:15,868 --> 00:07:18,271
I'm looking into those workers now, but…

111
00:07:19,572 --> 00:07:20,807
What's wrong?

112
00:07:23,876 --> 00:07:25,044
Nothing.

113
00:07:30,416 --> 00:07:31,350
Are you okay?

114
00:07:33,453 --> 00:07:34,654
Shall I call Dr. Yoshino?

115
00:07:36,222 --> 00:07:37,223
Water.

116
00:07:37,990 --> 00:07:38,825
Water?

117
00:07:41,327 --> 00:07:42,695
Let me…

118
00:07:42,762 --> 00:07:44,630
Excuse me.

119
00:07:48,868 --> 00:07:49,936
Here you go.

120
00:07:51,070 --> 00:07:52,138
Okay.

121
00:07:53,539 --> 00:07:54,841
I'll put this back.

122
00:08:01,647 --> 00:08:02,715
Thank you.

123
00:08:02,782 --> 00:08:03,749
You're welcome.

124
00:08:05,351 --> 00:08:08,721
Mister, did you know my mommy well?

125
00:08:09,455 --> 00:08:10,389
What?

126
00:08:12,558 --> 00:08:13,926
Not as well as you.

127
00:08:14,594 --> 00:08:17,730
What was she like at work?

128
00:08:21,968 --> 00:08:25,538
She did what she was asked,
and she did it well.

129
00:08:27,673 --> 00:08:30,276
When you do something well,
the person who asked you is happy.

130
00:08:31,077 --> 00:08:33,880
She liked seeing people happy.

131
00:08:34,614 --> 00:08:36,816
So I think she was a good person.

132
00:08:50,429 --> 00:08:51,898
What do you like about your mom?

133
00:08:54,133 --> 00:08:55,568
There are too many things.

134
00:08:56,669 --> 00:08:57,970
Figures.

135
00:09:11,484 --> 00:09:12,985
Sorry.

136
00:09:13,853 --> 00:09:16,622
Hang on. Hold this for a bit.

137
00:09:18,391 --> 00:09:19,425
What's wrong?

138
00:09:19,492 --> 00:09:21,761
Sorry, Nono has a nosebleed.

139
00:09:21,827 --> 00:09:23,029
I'm on my way.

140
00:09:24,497 --> 00:09:27,166
Did you take money from Nao?

141
00:09:28,568 --> 00:09:30,503
You were with Nao in Tokyo.

142
00:09:31,637 --> 00:09:32,538
Yes.

143
00:09:33,172 --> 00:09:34,206
Did he give you money?

144
00:09:34,273 --> 00:09:35,241
No.

145
00:09:35,308 --> 00:09:37,376
If he offers any, do not take it.

146
00:09:37,944 --> 00:09:41,847
Did someone sell
investigation details before?

147
00:09:42,915 --> 00:09:46,519
During the fake family suicide case,
there was such talk.

148
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:50,189
I was the first one they suspected,
because I had just bought a house.

149
00:09:50,256 --> 00:09:52,358
People do make up stupid rumors.

150
00:09:52,925 --> 00:09:54,860
If Mr. Nao was buying information,

151
00:09:54,927 --> 00:09:57,263
he wouldn't have
to bother people so brazenly.

152
00:09:57,330 --> 00:09:58,531
CHIKA - CALL ME

153
00:09:58,598 --> 00:09:59,565
Stay vigilant.

154
00:09:59,632 --> 00:10:02,134
You're too trusting for a detective.

155
00:10:02,201 --> 00:10:05,438
No, I'm growing as a person, too.

156
00:10:06,439 --> 00:10:10,509
Once you have doubted everything,
what remains is the truth.

157
00:10:12,878 --> 00:10:15,114
-Excuse me.
-Did you drink that much?

158
00:10:18,484 --> 00:10:19,585
Hey!

159
00:10:20,219 --> 00:10:21,187
Sorry.

160
00:10:21,253 --> 00:10:22,989
What are you doing?

161
00:10:25,458 --> 00:10:27,159
-Should I call an ambulance?
-Yes, hurry!

162
00:10:28,594 --> 00:10:31,831
Ogoma! Hey, stay with me! Ogoma!
Call an ambulance!

163
00:10:32,398 --> 00:10:35,701
There's something
I would like you to look at.

164
00:10:56,856 --> 00:10:58,357
Mr. Awashima.

165
00:11:00,526 --> 00:11:01,961
We were drinking--

166
00:11:02,828 --> 00:11:04,230
Lie down.

167
00:11:08,734 --> 00:11:10,236
Your drink…

168
00:11:10,803 --> 00:11:12,371
I passed it to Forensics to check.

169
00:11:12,438 --> 00:11:14,073
You said it tasted different.

170
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:17,043
Forensics? You're taking this too far.

171
00:11:19,845 --> 00:11:21,380
Was there anything in it?

172
00:11:22,014 --> 00:11:22,948
No.

173
00:11:23,649 --> 00:11:26,252
But there was something in your blood.

174
00:11:27,153 --> 00:11:28,521
What?

175
00:11:28,587 --> 00:11:29,455
Colchicine.

176
00:11:31,357 --> 00:11:32,458
It's poison, right?

177
00:11:32,525 --> 00:11:34,827
Two years ago,
Sakagami's grandpa was hospitalized

178
00:11:34,894 --> 00:11:36,962
after eating autumn crocus
on the mountain.

179
00:11:37,029 --> 00:11:38,297
Yeah.

180
00:11:38,931 --> 00:11:42,168
He mistook it for wild garlic.

181
00:11:42,234 --> 00:11:44,236
Any later, he would have died.

182
00:11:44,303 --> 00:11:45,438
You too.

183
00:11:53,779 --> 00:11:55,214
Did I eat something?

184
00:11:55,281 --> 00:11:58,751
No. The cause wasn't that restaurant.
It was earlier.

185
00:11:59,952 --> 00:12:03,122
Tell me what you ate and drank
since yesterday morning.

186
00:12:04,090 --> 00:12:05,091
Okay.

187
00:12:06,258 --> 00:12:07,093
One extra large bowl!

188
00:12:07,159 --> 00:12:12,331
I woke after noon,
ate meat udon at the station,

189
00:12:13,299 --> 00:12:17,536
went to the hospital, met Dr. Yoshino,

190
00:12:18,337 --> 00:12:19,472
I had coffee.

191
00:12:19,538 --> 00:12:20,372
What time?

192
00:12:22,208 --> 00:12:25,344
Around 4:00 p.m.

193
00:12:25,411 --> 00:12:26,245
Anything else?

194
00:12:26,312 --> 00:12:29,915
Then I had coffee at the hospital again.

195
00:12:29,982 --> 00:12:31,083
Mr. Nao bought it.

196
00:12:31,717 --> 00:12:34,120
It was vending machine coffee.

197
00:12:34,186 --> 00:12:35,254
Why Nao?

198
00:12:35,821 --> 00:12:37,423
He was with me then.

199
00:12:37,490 --> 00:12:39,625
An officer shouldn't just drink
what people give him!

200
00:12:39,692 --> 00:12:40,626
It's a courtesy.

201
00:12:40,693 --> 00:12:41,527
That's the problem.

202
00:12:42,094 --> 00:12:44,430
-Sorry.
-Must be the vending machine.

203
00:12:44,497 --> 00:12:46,065
I'll get them to shut it down.

204
00:12:50,803 --> 00:12:52,638
Poison?

205
00:12:55,274 --> 00:12:56,809
I need to call Mr. Nao.

206
00:12:58,711 --> 00:13:01,247
The person you have dialed…

207
00:13:01,313 --> 00:13:03,015
Hey, pick up!

208
00:13:03,082 --> 00:13:05,017
Please leave a message…

209
00:13:06,285 --> 00:13:08,420
Mr. Nao, are you okay?

210
00:13:08,487 --> 00:13:10,723
The hospital vending machine
may be a health risk.

211
00:13:14,927 --> 00:13:17,163
Think.

212
00:13:19,732 --> 00:13:21,400
I don't know.

213
00:13:36,415 --> 00:13:37,316
Mr. Nao.

214
00:13:39,185 --> 00:13:40,319
Mr. Nao.

215
00:13:41,420 --> 00:13:42,254
Mr. Nao--

216
00:13:45,291 --> 00:13:46,926
Seriously?

217
00:13:47,493 --> 00:13:48,360
Mr. Nao!

218
00:13:48,427 --> 00:13:50,162
This is the Shikara Police Station.

219
00:13:50,229 --> 00:13:51,697
Is this Mr. Nao's phone?

220
00:13:51,764 --> 00:13:55,568
We suspect someone
broke into your apartment.

221
00:13:57,036 --> 00:14:00,039
-Let's go with the black drawer.
-The drawer.

222
00:14:01,140 --> 00:14:03,709
Sorry I'm late.

223
00:14:03,776 --> 00:14:05,010
Mr. Nao.

224
00:14:06,111 --> 00:14:07,613
Are you feeling okay?

225
00:14:08,247 --> 00:14:09,081
Wow.

226
00:14:09,815 --> 00:14:12,585
This is terrible.

227
00:14:12,651 --> 00:14:14,553
Check to see if they took anything.

228
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:15,821
Okay.

229
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:24,930
Was anything taken?

230
00:14:25,497 --> 00:14:27,166
No.

231
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:30,135
I always carry valuables with me.

232
00:14:30,202 --> 00:14:32,805
If you have a damage report,
I can sign it.

233
00:14:32,872 --> 00:14:34,473
I'm writing it now.

234
00:14:36,508 --> 00:14:39,078
I have urgent work, so excuse me.

235
00:14:39,144 --> 00:14:40,246
Mr. Nao!

236
00:14:42,248 --> 00:14:43,749
-I'm going after him.
-Hey.

237
00:14:44,717 --> 00:14:45,818
Mr. Nao!

238
00:14:47,019 --> 00:14:48,153
Mr. Nao.

239
00:14:48,921 --> 00:14:51,690
Any idea why your place was broken into?

240
00:14:51,757 --> 00:14:52,691
I don't know.

241
00:14:52,758 --> 00:14:54,026
Maybe a thief?

242
00:14:54,093 --> 00:14:56,562
Only your place was hit.

243
00:14:56,629 --> 00:14:59,064
What happened
with the hospital vending machine?

244
00:14:59,131 --> 00:15:01,533
It seems there was no problem
with the machine itself.

245
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:03,535
Didn't someone get sick from it?

246
00:15:04,103 --> 00:15:04,970
Yes, I did.

247
00:15:05,638 --> 00:15:06,772
You did?

248
00:15:07,539 --> 00:15:08,574
Are you okay?

249
00:15:09,508 --> 00:15:11,310
I just ate something weird somewhere.

250
00:15:13,212 --> 00:15:15,981
Maybe in Tokyo? Did you try something new?

251
00:15:16,048 --> 00:15:17,283
Any idea why your place--

252
00:15:17,349 --> 00:15:18,584
I don't have any!

253
00:15:19,118 --> 00:15:21,053
Keep up the good work patrolling.

254
00:15:25,891 --> 00:15:27,259
Oh, hello.

255
00:15:33,699 --> 00:15:35,834
Yes, understood.

256
00:15:39,171 --> 00:15:40,072
See you.

257
00:15:57,756 --> 00:15:59,758
-Here.
-Thank you.

258
00:16:01,860 --> 00:16:02,895
Ms. Aya.

259
00:16:03,696 --> 00:16:05,097
Thank you for coming here.

260
00:16:05,164 --> 00:16:08,600
You came with me
to Tetsu's grave after all.

261
00:16:08,667 --> 00:16:10,402
We seem to meet often.

262
00:16:10,936 --> 00:16:12,137
We do.

263
00:16:15,174 --> 00:16:16,542
Shall we go somewhere else?

264
00:16:16,608 --> 00:16:18,477
-Oh, it's fine. No one is around.
-No.

265
00:16:18,544 --> 00:16:19,979
I saw someone weird.

266
00:16:23,515 --> 00:16:24,416
Nobori.

267
00:16:25,050 --> 00:16:27,519
This is Ogoma. From Shikara Police.

268
00:16:28,187 --> 00:16:29,455
-Huh?
-What?

269
00:16:29,521 --> 00:16:31,056
Are you really Ogoma?

270
00:16:31,123 --> 00:16:32,257
What?

271
00:16:32,324 --> 00:16:33,692
You've changed.

272
00:16:33,759 --> 00:16:35,461
You used to look like a bad guy.

273
00:16:36,028 --> 00:16:38,864
I always avoided him,
thinking he might shake me down.

274
00:16:38,931 --> 00:16:40,866
Don't talk like he's a mad dog.

275
00:16:40,933 --> 00:16:42,134
He's my student, after all.

276
00:16:43,235 --> 00:16:47,172
He acts cool, but Nobori's family home
is actually near that town too.

277
00:16:47,239 --> 00:16:48,440
I see.

278
00:16:48,507 --> 00:16:50,142
I have no good memories of it,

279
00:16:50,809 --> 00:16:53,145
but seeing you, I feel a bit nostalgic.

280
00:16:55,647 --> 00:16:56,548
You're a president?

281
00:16:56,615 --> 00:16:57,816
It's a small company.

282
00:16:57,883 --> 00:16:59,084
It's not that small.

283
00:16:59,151 --> 00:17:00,586
He has a shop in Tokyo too.

284
00:17:00,652 --> 00:17:01,487
A shop?

285
00:17:01,553 --> 00:17:04,790
Selling cosmetics,
made from Hokkaido plants.

286
00:17:04,857 --> 00:17:09,395
Like lavender, beach rose,
sea buckthorn, calendula?

287
00:17:09,461 --> 00:17:10,362
Cale…

288
00:17:10,429 --> 00:17:11,397
-Calendula.
-Aya.

289
00:17:11,997 --> 00:17:13,565
We can talk about that later.

290
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:16,702
-Shall we go somewhere else?
-Yes.

291
00:17:28,447 --> 00:17:31,417
I found this in school.

292
00:17:38,157 --> 00:17:39,558
It goes by the name "CAN-d."

293
00:17:40,793 --> 00:17:42,127
CAN-d?

294
00:17:44,897 --> 00:17:48,167
Nobori, how are you involved with this…

295
00:17:48,233 --> 00:17:51,970
She asked me
to analyze this drug in my lab.

296
00:17:54,039 --> 00:17:56,175
It's an opioid-type drug.

297
00:17:56,241 --> 00:17:59,244
Made of an ingredient
not yet regulated in Japan.

298
00:18:03,148 --> 00:18:05,717
Was a student carrying this?

299
00:18:06,919 --> 00:18:08,987
It was found in our club room.

300
00:18:09,688 --> 00:18:11,290
I don't know who brought it in.

301
00:18:13,092 --> 00:18:16,328
Many students at Aya's middle school
go on to elite schools

302
00:18:16,395 --> 00:18:18,030
in Sapporo and Hakodate.

303
00:18:18,097 --> 00:18:21,467
Whoever brought
this in should be punished.

304
00:18:22,434 --> 00:18:28,240
I asked Nobori to analyze it,
and then thought I should call the police.

305
00:18:31,343 --> 00:18:34,246
I know some knowledgeable people.
I'll take this to them.

306
00:18:34,947 --> 00:18:36,315
Thank you.

307
00:18:36,381 --> 00:18:37,850
May I keep this?

308
00:18:38,650 --> 00:18:39,485
Yes.

309
00:18:45,424 --> 00:18:48,560
Are you in charge of this matter, Ms. Aya?

310
00:18:49,128 --> 00:18:50,129
Yes.

311
00:18:51,096 --> 00:18:55,100
Our school almost never
gets into problems with the police.

312
00:18:56,235 --> 00:18:59,204
The principal and head teacher
are at a loss.

313
00:18:59,271 --> 00:19:03,308
Suspecting each student
is a heavy burden for a teacher.

314
00:19:04,676 --> 00:19:06,411
You don't want to suspect them.

315
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:09,414
But…

316
00:19:10,182 --> 00:19:14,853
because you believed in me,
I'm here without having been to juvy.

317
00:19:17,422 --> 00:19:20,859
Without you,
I would be in a gang or something.

318
00:19:27,799 --> 00:19:31,336
Many children died from this drug.

319
00:19:34,273 --> 00:19:36,175
Not just delinquents.

320
00:19:37,643 --> 00:19:39,011
Even good kids too.

321
00:19:42,614 --> 00:19:44,483
Some of them are students.

322
00:19:52,658 --> 00:19:56,395
For now, we should doubt, not trust.

323
00:19:57,563 --> 00:20:00,766
I think it will help
prevent people from dying.

324
00:20:04,503 --> 00:20:06,605
We will be able to save lives, right?

325
00:20:10,609 --> 00:20:12,444
Thanks for reporting it.

326
00:20:17,883 --> 00:20:20,953
I heard you cleared Aya of suspicion.

327
00:20:21,787 --> 00:20:23,488
Well, I guess so.

328
00:20:23,555 --> 00:20:24,790
Thanks.

329
00:20:25,324 --> 00:20:27,059
Isn't it weird for me to thank you?

330
00:20:27,125 --> 00:20:28,126
It is, yes.

331
00:20:28,927 --> 00:20:32,497
Our company sometimes holds
nature classes in the mountains.

332
00:20:33,031 --> 00:20:35,434
We meet middle
and high school students often,

333
00:20:35,500 --> 00:20:37,736
so if I can help, I'll do anything.

334
00:20:37,803 --> 00:20:39,805
Oh, that would be great.

335
00:20:42,140 --> 00:20:43,475
I never shook anyone down.

336
00:20:43,542 --> 00:20:45,143
-Never, really?
-Never.

337
00:20:45,210 --> 00:20:47,646
He would never shake people down. Right?

338
00:20:47,713 --> 00:20:50,015
I would never! What's with the two of you?

339
00:20:50,082 --> 00:20:50,916
Bye.

340
00:20:50,983 --> 00:20:52,451
-Bye, Ogoma.
-I'll call you.

341
00:20:52,517 --> 00:20:55,120
-Okay! Let's go.
-Hey, you have your own umbrella.

342
00:20:56,722 --> 00:20:58,257
Umbrellas are a pain.

343
00:20:58,323 --> 00:20:59,291
See you!

344
00:20:59,358 --> 00:21:00,359
Bye!

345
00:21:12,537 --> 00:21:14,373
Are you feeling okay, Mr. Ogoma?

346
00:21:14,439 --> 00:21:15,841
I'm completely fine.

347
00:21:16,475 --> 00:21:20,579
I would like to ask Dr. Yoshino
about when he bought the coffee.

348
00:21:20,646 --> 00:21:23,048
He's busy right now.

349
00:21:23,115 --> 00:21:24,283
-Yes?
-Look.

350
00:21:26,918 --> 00:21:28,320
Mr. Nao?

351
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:35,560
I checked the analysis results you sent.

352
00:21:35,627 --> 00:21:37,262
The ingredients are basically CAN-d.

353
00:21:37,329 --> 00:21:40,065
I thought we had cracked down
and stopped the flow,

354
00:21:40,132 --> 00:21:41,566
but it's circulating again.

355
00:21:41,633 --> 00:21:43,135
Has it been found elsewhere?

356
00:21:43,201 --> 00:21:45,737
Last month. In Tokyo and Yokohama.

357
00:21:46,605 --> 00:21:48,373
You heard about the money, right?

358
00:21:49,708 --> 00:21:50,809
What money?

359
00:21:50,876 --> 00:21:52,644
The money found in that sublet.

360
00:21:54,713 --> 00:21:56,315
What are you talking about?

361
00:21:57,616 --> 00:21:59,451
Didn't the insurance man tell you?

362
00:22:00,819 --> 00:22:01,720
No.

363
00:22:01,787 --> 00:22:02,721
Then never mind.

364
00:22:02,788 --> 00:22:05,257
Hey, you brought it up. Just tell me.

365
00:22:16,268 --> 00:22:17,269
Mr. Nao!

366
00:22:18,203 --> 00:22:19,438
We keep meeting today.

367
00:22:19,504 --> 00:22:21,840
Mr. Nao, can we talk?

368
00:22:21,907 --> 00:22:23,608
-I'm busy.
-Five minutes.

369
00:22:23,675 --> 00:22:24,776
What?

370
00:22:28,080 --> 00:22:29,815
You hiding something from me?

371
00:22:31,583 --> 00:22:33,118
You didn't poison me, right?

372
00:22:35,887 --> 00:22:38,056
That's a shockingly rude question.

373
00:22:38,123 --> 00:22:40,559
Will you ask Dr. Yoshino the same thing?

374
00:22:40,625 --> 00:22:42,594
You should think about how you say it.

375
00:22:43,628 --> 00:22:45,497
-And…
-There's more?

376
00:22:46,031 --> 00:22:48,100
The money from that illegal sublet.

377
00:22:50,302 --> 00:22:51,269
What was he talking about?

378
00:22:51,770 --> 00:22:53,538
Sublet money?

379
00:22:54,139 --> 00:22:56,775
-That is…
-Yes?

380
00:22:58,143 --> 00:22:59,478
Sorry, I'm in a hurry.

381
00:22:59,544 --> 00:23:01,747
Why are you sneaking around?

382
00:23:02,247 --> 00:23:04,549
I need you to tell me honestly
what you know.

383
00:23:04,616 --> 00:23:05,550
I'm being honest.

384
00:23:05,617 --> 00:23:08,253
You were the one who told me
to doubt everything.

385
00:23:09,855 --> 00:23:10,689
Not now.

386
00:23:10,756 --> 00:23:12,057
-Nao!
-Cut it out.

387
00:23:16,428 --> 00:23:18,163
I'll come see you later!

388
00:23:18,697 --> 00:23:20,399
I'll have you come to the station.

389
00:23:28,006 --> 00:23:29,474
Hello.

390
00:23:30,776 --> 00:23:32,210
Hello.

391
00:23:32,277 --> 00:23:34,212
Is Dr. Yoshino free now?

392
00:23:34,279 --> 00:23:36,381
Huh? He's out.

393
00:23:36,948 --> 00:23:39,151
Where did he go? He was just here.

394
00:23:39,217 --> 00:23:40,619
-A house call.
-A house call?

395
00:23:40,685 --> 00:23:43,288
He probably won't be back today.

396
00:23:43,355 --> 00:23:44,689
Seriously…

397
00:23:46,057 --> 00:23:47,359
For real?

398
00:23:48,360 --> 00:23:50,896
Got it. Thank you.

399
00:24:09,114 --> 00:24:10,248
Mr. Awashima?

400
00:24:13,452 --> 00:24:14,386
Yes?

401
00:24:15,053 --> 00:24:17,255
Ogoma, how are you feeling?

402
00:24:19,257 --> 00:24:20,926
I'm completely fine.

403
00:24:20,992 --> 00:24:25,530
Since then, we've split up and watched
the people who gave you drinks.

404
00:24:26,331 --> 00:24:29,000
Mr. Nao and Dr. Yoshino?

405
00:24:29,067 --> 00:24:30,368
What's their relationship?

406
00:24:33,705 --> 00:24:38,977
Mr. Nao often consults with the doctor
about insurance matters.

407
00:24:39,044 --> 00:24:40,245
He was at the hospital today too.

408
00:24:40,312 --> 00:24:41,613
Did they talk?

409
00:24:41,680 --> 00:24:42,581
Yes.

410
00:24:42,647 --> 00:24:43,482
When?

411
00:24:43,548 --> 00:24:44,516
When?

412
00:24:49,120 --> 00:24:51,456
About four or five hours ago.

413
00:24:51,523 --> 00:24:52,791
They're talking again.

414
00:24:54,359 --> 00:24:55,193
Huh?

415
00:24:56,094 --> 00:24:57,162
They're talking again.

416
00:24:57,229 --> 00:24:58,363
Nao and Yoshino.

417
00:25:01,566 --> 00:25:02,601
Again?

418
00:25:16,515 --> 00:25:18,250
It's true.

419
00:25:29,494 --> 00:25:30,328
Huh?

420
00:25:30,996 --> 00:25:33,098
Did they have a fight?

421
00:25:38,537 --> 00:25:39,704
Which one?

422
00:25:39,771 --> 00:25:41,339
I'll chase after Nao.

423
00:26:01,927 --> 00:26:03,528
This is so difficult.

424
00:26:12,837 --> 00:26:13,838
Huh?

425
00:26:14,739 --> 00:26:15,574
Mr. Nao!

426
00:26:16,074 --> 00:26:18,176
Mr. Nao, why are you running?

427
00:26:18,243 --> 00:26:20,712
Mr. Nao! Why are you running?

428
00:26:21,446 --> 00:26:22,347
Mr. Nao!

429
00:26:28,186 --> 00:26:29,187
Seriously?

430
00:26:50,942 --> 00:26:52,711
24 HOURS EARLIER

431
00:27:02,087 --> 00:27:03,722
It's okay now. It stopped.

432
00:27:05,991 --> 00:27:07,926
I'll come check on you again.

433
00:27:12,931 --> 00:27:17,802
VISITOR'S PASS

434
00:27:18,837 --> 00:27:21,539
I must tell you something about my sister.

435
00:27:23,441 --> 00:27:24,643
Are you going home?

436
00:27:25,243 --> 00:27:26,077
Huh?

437
00:27:27,345 --> 00:27:28,346
I'm still here.

438
00:27:29,014 --> 00:27:30,915
What were we talking about?

439
00:28:02,747 --> 00:28:04,449
Hello, it's Nao.

440
00:28:04,516 --> 00:28:05,650
Um…

441
00:28:06,317 --> 00:28:08,920
There's something
I would like you to look at.

442
00:28:12,791 --> 00:28:14,826
10 HOURS EARLIER

443
00:28:16,227 --> 00:28:17,595
Hey, Nao.

444
00:28:17,662 --> 00:28:19,798
Are you looking
into Motoka Tabatake's insurance?

445
00:28:19,864 --> 00:28:22,934
I explained everything to you
when I was in Tokyo.

446
00:28:23,001 --> 00:28:24,736
I'm only giving advice.

447
00:28:24,803 --> 00:28:25,870
You aren't thinking of

448
00:28:25,937 --> 00:28:28,840
trying to get the insurance paid
to the daughter, are you?

449
00:28:28,907 --> 00:28:30,542
You must not get directly involved.

450
00:28:30,608 --> 00:28:32,877
I would never do that.

451
00:28:32,944 --> 00:28:36,114
-Follow professional ethics at all times.
-Sure.

452
00:28:36,181 --> 00:28:38,983
Sure, sure.

453
00:28:40,685 --> 00:28:42,020
So annoying.

454
00:28:45,857 --> 00:28:46,858
Excuse me.

455
00:28:46,925 --> 00:28:49,294
Sorry for making you come all this way.

456
00:28:49,360 --> 00:28:50,495
Here, I brought you this.

457
00:28:50,562 --> 00:28:52,297
-Thank you!
-What?

458
00:28:52,363 --> 00:28:54,766
-What is it?
-Jaga Pokkuru.

459
00:28:56,835 --> 00:28:58,470
I can't leave the house easily.

460
00:28:58,536 --> 00:28:59,404
Yes.

461
00:29:00,138 --> 00:29:01,072
I understand.

462
00:29:01,139 --> 00:29:02,273
Sorry.

463
00:29:05,443 --> 00:29:07,712
Is this your sister's?

464
00:29:07,779 --> 00:29:08,780
Yes.

465
00:29:08,847 --> 00:29:10,582
They said it was in Nono's hospital room.

466
00:29:10,648 --> 00:29:11,483
Where's my water bottle?

467
00:29:11,549 --> 00:29:12,517
Over there.

468
00:29:13,651 --> 00:29:15,520
I don't know the lock number.

469
00:29:16,788 --> 00:29:18,256
Excuse me.

470
00:29:19,324 --> 00:29:20,191
There!

471
00:29:23,528 --> 00:29:25,263
Is this your sister's handwriting?

472
00:29:27,465 --> 00:29:28,366
Yes.

473
00:29:30,168 --> 00:29:32,303
-Want to read it?
-No. You first.

474
00:29:33,304 --> 00:29:35,707
I'm scared of what might be in it.

475
00:29:40,278 --> 00:29:41,246
Allow me.

476
00:29:49,487 --> 00:29:51,823
Is it a diary?

477
00:29:53,358 --> 00:29:55,527
Not really.

478
00:29:55,593 --> 00:29:57,162
More like a memo.

479
00:29:57,228 --> 00:29:58,897
A record of sorts.

480
00:30:00,832 --> 00:30:04,302
The first entry is from August last year.

481
00:30:05,470 --> 00:30:06,437
Hey…

482
00:30:08,006 --> 00:30:09,140
Is there a will?

483
00:30:09,207 --> 00:30:10,041
A will?

484
00:30:10,108 --> 00:30:11,042
Yes.

485
00:30:13,344 --> 00:30:14,779
Let me see…

486
00:30:18,683 --> 00:30:20,552
No, doesn't seem to be.

487
00:30:20,618 --> 00:30:23,922
She appears to have worked as usual
until the day she died.

488
00:30:25,924 --> 00:30:27,192
I knew it.

489
00:30:28,893 --> 00:30:30,628
It wasn't suicide, right?

490
00:30:33,298 --> 00:30:36,568
I would have to read all of this
before I say anything.

491
00:30:38,803 --> 00:30:40,171
I was happy.

492
00:30:41,406 --> 00:30:42,874
That you decided to help us.

493
00:30:44,108 --> 00:30:47,846
I have no money and can't do anything.

494
00:30:48,980 --> 00:30:51,249
I don't want to lose Nono too.

495
00:30:52,750 --> 00:30:55,653
Please, help me.

496
00:31:00,758 --> 00:31:02,627
Let me ask you one thing.

497
00:31:04,762 --> 00:31:08,466
Have the police told you anything…

498
00:31:09,467 --> 00:31:10,401
about your sister?

499
00:31:10,468 --> 00:31:15,206
My sister wasn't involved
in any crime, was she?

500
00:31:18,042 --> 00:31:19,611
I can't say for sure.

501
00:31:24,449 --> 00:31:26,451
But as a general rule,

502
00:31:28,519 --> 00:31:31,723
even if the insured
was involved in a crime,

503
00:31:32,590 --> 00:31:35,093
insurance is usually still paid.

504
00:31:35,159 --> 00:31:38,296
However, if the insured or the recipient

505
00:31:38,363 --> 00:31:41,566
was involved with criminal
or terrorist groups,

506
00:31:42,533 --> 00:31:46,070
the contract can be canceled.

507
00:31:47,772 --> 00:31:50,308
Then the insurance wouldn't be paid?

508
00:31:50,375 --> 00:31:51,476
That's right.

509
00:31:59,717 --> 00:32:02,687
First, let's read this.

510
00:32:02,754 --> 00:32:03,588
Yes.

511
00:32:07,191 --> 00:32:08,726
August 4th.

512
00:32:09,494 --> 00:32:11,396
Dr. Yoshino contacted me.

513
00:32:12,130 --> 00:32:13,898
Nono's fever won't go down.

514
00:32:15,500 --> 00:32:18,770
No appetite, swollen lymph nodes.

515
00:32:18,836 --> 00:32:20,738
Her symptoms have worsened.

516
00:32:22,407 --> 00:32:26,210
Dr. Yoshino proposes
a change in treatment.

517
00:32:27,011 --> 00:32:30,715
The current medicine
isn't enough to control the fever.

518
00:32:33,251 --> 00:32:36,287
The new drug is not approved in Japan.

519
00:32:37,155 --> 00:32:38,489
Fully out of pocket.

520
00:32:39,023 --> 00:32:41,259
The system won't cover it.

521
00:32:42,327 --> 00:32:44,762
WELFARE

522
00:32:47,832 --> 00:32:49,767
INCOME
OUTGOING EXPENSES

523
00:32:49,834 --> 00:32:51,769
MEDICAL LOANS

524
00:32:51,836 --> 00:32:53,771
CROWDFUNDING

525
00:32:54,806 --> 00:32:56,975
I was introduced to a delivery job.

526
00:32:57,842 --> 00:32:58,943
The client,

527
00:32:59,711 --> 00:33:00,745
a Mr. Tsugaru.

528
00:33:03,114 --> 00:33:04,048
Tsugaru.

529
00:33:07,185 --> 00:33:09,587
Test results are improving.

530
00:33:10,221 --> 00:33:12,156
Dr. Yoshino and I were so happy.

531
00:33:12,824 --> 00:33:13,825
I cried.

532
00:33:14,859 --> 00:33:16,494
Today was a good day.

533
00:33:17,729 --> 00:33:20,298
We'll continue
until gene therapy is possible.

534
00:33:20,365 --> 00:33:23,534
I have no choice
but to continue the Tsugaru job.

535
00:33:27,839 --> 00:33:29,640
Another 300,000 yen came in.

536
00:33:30,541 --> 00:33:32,577
For only two or three deliveries a month.

537
00:33:34,712 --> 00:33:36,781
Am I really doing the right thing?

538
00:33:38,516 --> 00:33:40,852
Would Nono be sad over me doing this?

539
00:33:45,256 --> 00:33:47,191
I made a mountain delivery again.

540
00:33:47,258 --> 00:33:48,393
The same thing.

541
00:33:50,795 --> 00:33:52,697
This isn't a normal part-time job.

542
00:33:53,931 --> 00:33:55,933
I'm probably doing something bad.

543
00:34:01,072 --> 00:34:02,640
When I said I wanted to quit,

544
00:34:03,207 --> 00:34:06,044
he told me,
"Who would be in trouble if you quit?"

545
00:34:07,378 --> 00:34:08,379
It's me.

546
00:34:12,183 --> 00:34:14,318
I can't let Nono know I'm in trouble.

547
00:34:15,420 --> 00:34:18,056
Nono is in more pain than I am,
because of her illness.

548
00:34:20,491 --> 00:34:22,627
I'm glad Nono was born.

549
00:34:23,928 --> 00:34:25,997
She's my greatest joy.

550
00:34:29,634 --> 00:34:32,503
I must see Nono grow up.

551
00:34:33,905 --> 00:34:35,473
Whatever it takes.

552
00:34:36,874 --> 00:34:39,811
I WILL PROTECT HER

553
00:34:47,618 --> 00:34:48,820
I love you.

554
00:34:49,520 --> 00:34:50,421
I love you.

555
00:34:51,022 --> 00:34:52,690
What do you like about your mom?

556
00:34:53,357 --> 00:34:54,959
There are too many things.

557
00:35:01,866 --> 00:35:02,800
So…

558
00:35:03,534 --> 00:35:04,936
How is it?

559
00:35:05,837 --> 00:35:09,974
If the police see this,
it will prove she didn't kill herself--

560
00:35:10,041 --> 00:35:11,209
Wait, wait.

561
00:35:11,275 --> 00:35:12,610
Wait a moment.

562
00:35:12,677 --> 00:35:13,878
We can't really…

563
00:35:18,082 --> 00:35:20,351
About the notebook…

564
00:35:21,786 --> 00:35:25,523
Please don't tell anyone
about it for a while.

565
00:35:27,125 --> 00:35:28,626
Don't tell the police, either.

566
00:35:33,764 --> 00:35:35,032
Is this Mr. Nao's phone?

567
00:35:35,099 --> 00:35:36,267
Yes, hello.

568
00:35:36,334 --> 00:35:39,704
We suspect someone
broke into your apartment.

569
00:35:39,770 --> 00:35:40,605
Huh?

570
00:35:42,206 --> 00:35:43,040
An intruder?

571
00:35:46,110 --> 00:35:46,978
Huh?

572
00:35:49,046 --> 00:35:51,983
A SHADY PART-TIME JOB?
IS TSUGARU PART OF A GANG?

573
00:35:58,322 --> 00:35:59,790
Was anything taken?

574
00:36:00,892 --> 00:36:02,493
No.

575
00:36:03,060 --> 00:36:05,396
If you have a damage report,
I can sign it.

576
00:36:05,463 --> 00:36:07,365
I'm writing it now.

577
00:36:16,841 --> 00:36:19,243
Someone broke into my place? Why?

578
00:36:20,044 --> 00:36:21,812
I'm scared.

579
00:36:23,848 --> 00:36:24,849
Mr. Nao.

580
00:36:26,117 --> 00:36:27,118
Mr. Nao!

581
00:36:28,853 --> 00:36:31,322
Any idea why your place was broken into?

582
00:36:31,389 --> 00:36:32,323
I don't know.

583
00:36:32,390 --> 00:36:34,825
DR. YOSHINO

584
00:36:37,562 --> 00:36:38,829
Oh, hello.

585
00:36:39,330 --> 00:36:42,433
I know you called me,
but I have an afternoon consultation.

586
00:36:42,500 --> 00:36:45,069
I can see you around 3:00 p.m.

587
00:36:45,136 --> 00:36:46,804
Then see you later.

588
00:36:50,341 --> 00:36:51,342
See you.

589
00:36:55,146 --> 00:36:56,714
Where is Mommy?

590
00:36:58,516 --> 00:36:59,884
She died?

591
00:37:01,152 --> 00:37:02,286
Why?

592
00:37:06,724 --> 00:37:09,660
THE TREATMENT HAS RISKS, THOUGH SMALL,
THE DOCTOR DOESN'T RECOMMEND IT

593
00:37:09,727 --> 00:37:11,128
TREATMENT NOT WORTH THE MONEY

594
00:37:11,195 --> 00:37:13,664
A normal person
can't earn this much a month.

595
00:37:13,731 --> 00:37:17,535
If the family can afford it,
we doctors will respect their wishes.

596
00:37:19,804 --> 00:37:21,272
Oh, thanks for waiting.

597
00:37:21,339 --> 00:37:23,741
Sorry for endlessly bothering you.

598
00:37:23,808 --> 00:37:26,644
Yesterday, Mr. Ogoma
was rushed to our hospital.

599
00:37:26,711 --> 00:37:29,447
They said he accidentally
swallowed poison.

600
00:37:30,948 --> 00:37:32,683
Are you okay, Nao?

601
00:37:32,750 --> 00:37:34,518
Yes, I'm fine.

602
00:37:35,786 --> 00:37:36,887
Thank goodness.

603
00:37:37,488 --> 00:37:39,590
-Was it about Nono's medical costs?
-Yes.

604
00:37:40,458 --> 00:37:42,093
Where did I…

605
00:37:43,327 --> 00:37:44,362
Excuse me.

606
00:37:44,996 --> 00:37:46,030
This is Yoshino.

607
00:37:46,097 --> 00:37:49,000
Doctor, could you come check
the test results?

608
00:37:49,533 --> 00:37:50,568
Coming.

609
00:37:51,435 --> 00:37:53,104
Sorry, I have to go.

610
00:37:53,170 --> 00:37:57,375
How about we have lunch
at a place you like?

611
00:37:57,441 --> 00:37:59,877
I must leave for house calls soon.

612
00:37:59,944 --> 00:38:01,078
What time?

613
00:38:01,145 --> 00:38:02,246
Let's see…

614
00:38:03,848 --> 00:38:05,416
You didn't poison me, right?

615
00:38:05,483 --> 00:38:08,586
Will you ask Dr. Yoshino the same thing?

616
00:38:08,653 --> 00:38:10,554
You should think about how you say it.

617
00:38:11,622 --> 00:38:14,125
-And…
-There's more?

618
00:38:14,925 --> 00:38:17,762
The money from that illegal sublet.

619
00:38:22,466 --> 00:38:25,036
What was he talking about?

620
00:38:25,603 --> 00:38:27,905
-That is…
-Yes?

621
00:38:32,376 --> 00:38:33,210
Not now.

622
00:38:33,277 --> 00:38:35,346
-Nao!
-Cut it out.

623
00:38:37,815 --> 00:38:39,617
I'll come see you later!

624
00:38:39,684 --> 00:38:41,285
I'll have you come to the station.

625
00:38:41,852 --> 00:38:43,120
Dr. Yoshino!

626
00:38:44,722 --> 00:38:46,257
Are you leaving for a house call?

627
00:38:46,824 --> 00:38:47,725
Yes.

628
00:38:51,195 --> 00:38:52,630
Did you drop something?

629
00:38:52,697 --> 00:38:53,564
Huh?

630
00:39:00,838 --> 00:39:02,606
This is yours.

631
00:39:02,673 --> 00:39:04,442
Huh? What?

632
00:39:04,508 --> 00:39:07,078
You're right. How did I drop it?

633
00:39:07,144 --> 00:39:08,646
See you later.

634
00:39:08,713 --> 00:39:09,847
Later.

635
00:39:16,921 --> 00:39:19,123
ONE HOUR EARLIER

636
00:39:23,461 --> 00:39:26,263
How is it going
with Ms. Tabatake's life insurance?

637
00:39:26,797 --> 00:39:28,466
Can Nono receive it?

638
00:39:28,532 --> 00:39:29,600
I would like…

639
00:39:30,568 --> 00:39:32,269
your opinion on that.

640
00:39:33,037 --> 00:39:34,138
The other day,

641
00:39:34,739 --> 00:39:37,575
we talked a bit
about Ms. Tabatake's financial situation.

642
00:39:37,641 --> 00:39:38,542
Yes.

643
00:39:38,609 --> 00:39:43,547
Someone told me that Ms. Tabatake
consulted you many times

644
00:39:43,614 --> 00:39:45,616
about medical costs, didn't she?

645
00:39:46,317 --> 00:39:51,355
For example, taking on medical loans,
clinical trials of unapproved drugs,

646
00:39:52,156 --> 00:39:56,427
systems combining insured and
uninsured care, crowdfunding, and so on.

647
00:39:57,161 --> 00:39:58,062
Yes.

648
00:39:58,796 --> 00:40:03,734
But you didn't approve of any of them.

649
00:40:04,502 --> 00:40:07,872
I didn't think
she should push herself financially.

650
00:40:08,672 --> 00:40:10,374
I suggested treatment within reason.

651
00:40:10,441 --> 00:40:14,812
Wasn't it you yourself who proposed
treatment with an unapproved drug?

652
00:40:17,748 --> 00:40:20,351
I didn't propose it. I just presented it.

653
00:40:20,418 --> 00:40:22,019
I was giving her options.

654
00:40:22,586 --> 00:40:24,789
Once treatment
with an unapproved drug starts,

655
00:40:24,855 --> 00:40:26,791
money is needed endlessly.

656
00:40:26,857 --> 00:40:29,260
For Nono, money is her life fuel.

657
00:40:30,694 --> 00:40:31,962
If it runs out, she dies.

658
00:40:32,830 --> 00:40:34,031
Right?

659
00:40:37,201 --> 00:40:40,271
I don't think I'm giving
the wrong treatment.

660
00:40:41,372 --> 00:40:45,342
I'm talking about money,
not her treatment.

661
00:40:51,982 --> 00:40:56,287
Ms. Tabatake also consulted you
about insured experimental trials, right?

662
00:40:56,921 --> 00:41:00,324
But you didn't even consider it.

663
00:41:00,391 --> 00:41:04,895
Why didn't you
give it a little bit of thought?

664
00:41:04,962 --> 00:41:06,530
As I said, pushing herself--

665
00:41:06,597 --> 00:41:10,701
You knew she would go ahead
with out-of-pocket treatment, right?

666
00:41:10,768 --> 00:41:13,003
It was Ms. Tabatake's decision
to work and raise money.

667
00:41:16,507 --> 00:41:21,078
Do you know how Ms. Tabatake covered…

668
00:41:22,680 --> 00:41:24,048
the treatment costs?

669
00:41:30,688 --> 00:41:34,959
From now on, please talk
with the hospital's social worker, not me.

670
00:41:36,560 --> 00:41:37,862
Excuse me.

671
00:41:54,245 --> 00:41:56,881
What is going on? Who is that?

672
00:41:56,947 --> 00:41:59,016
I'm scared.

673
00:41:59,783 --> 00:42:01,752
So scary.

674
00:42:02,486 --> 00:42:03,787
What do I do?

675
00:42:07,491 --> 00:42:08,759
Ogoma?

676
00:42:10,060 --> 00:42:13,531
-Why?
-Mr. Nao!

677
00:42:13,597 --> 00:42:16,500
-Why are you running?
-I don't know.

678
00:42:16,567 --> 00:42:17,568
Mr. Nao!

679
00:42:17,635 --> 00:42:20,604
This is bad! What do I do?

680
00:42:44,562 --> 00:42:47,031
Hey! Ogoma!

681
00:42:51,268 --> 00:42:53,237
Ogoma!

682
00:42:53,304 --> 00:42:55,839
What are you doing? Stop acting rashly.

683
00:42:55,906 --> 00:42:58,242
Here. Come on.

684
00:42:58,309 --> 00:42:59,410
There you go.

685
00:43:00,477 --> 00:43:03,614
I don't believe you.

686
00:43:05,182 --> 00:43:06,317
Take this off.

687
00:43:10,688 --> 00:43:12,990
What is this?

688
00:43:15,292 --> 00:43:16,594
I wonder…

689
00:43:16,660 --> 00:43:18,529
Why did you throw it away?

690
00:43:21,832 --> 00:43:24,201
Wait a moment. I'll bring the car around.

691
00:43:25,936 --> 00:43:27,905
-That hurts!
-Don't try to run.

692
00:43:27,972 --> 00:43:29,239
Come to the station.

693
00:43:43,053 --> 00:43:44,655
What are you thinking?

694
00:43:54,932 --> 00:43:56,266
Tell me everything.

695
00:43:56,333 --> 00:43:58,002
-The investigation files?
-He took something! What?

696
00:43:58,068 --> 00:43:58,836
Go after Ogoma.

697
00:43:58,902 --> 00:44:00,738
In all probability,
a person related to this case.

698
00:44:00,804 --> 00:44:04,408
It's all connected, right?
Everything since the mountain accident.

699
00:44:04,475 --> 00:44:05,843
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
